<title>NORWAY: UNI Storebrand drops UNI from name.</title>
<headline>UNI Storebrand drops UNI from name.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>UNI Storebrand ASA, Norway's largest insurance company, said on Monday it was shortening its company name to Storebrand ASA as part of a campaign to boost its image.</p>
<p>A statement said the company was dropping the word &quot;UNI&quot; as of Tuesday in line with an annual general meeting decision in May.</p>
<p>&quot;The purpose is to simplify the dialogue with customers and to build up a stronger brand-name identity,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
